    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside trio in the outfield, with **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) leading our efficiency rankings. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Martinez, while **Seiya Suzuki** is primed for a high-output game against the vulnerable Lauer, aided by a prime #2 hole placement. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) rounds out our top-tier group, capitalizing on a weak SP matchup against Lowder. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains a must-start at 66.43 despite facing a tougher arm in Mize; his stolen base potential remains the primary engine for our category scarcity strategy, even with a slight negative adjustment for the opponent's elite hold percentage.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Brice Turang** in the UTIL slot despite a daunting matchup against Skenes (47.32). While the score is marginally above our 40-point bench threshold, his leadoff spot and stolen base utility kept him ahead of **Cole Young** (36.38), who missed the cut due to his own unfavorable matchup against Anderson and a lower base projection. We are managing risk carefully with **Austin Riley**, whose score of 51.86 is suppressed by a bottom-of-the-order assignment, though we anticipate his power profile will capitalize on the pitcher's slower delivery to boost his stolen base probability. \n\nWe continue to monitor the status of our depth pieces, with **James Wood** still sidelined on the IL and **Jose Caballero** unavailable today. We are playing a cautious game with our total games played allocation; by benching both **Cole Young** and **Zach McKinstry**, we maintain the integrity of our efficiency-based bench floor. We are avoiding exposure to high-K environments like the one **Brice Turang** faces against Skenes if possible, but our current depth remains committed to the highest potential for Runs and SBs, keeping players like **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor** in the fold to provide stable counting stats despite moderate matchups against Mize and Anderson, respectively.",
